 tour the space, learn about services and community offerings, visit the Journal Pantry, connect with others, and register for the free Summer of Reflection Challenge, a four-week community journaling experience beginning June 29. When: Tuesday, June 23 | 11 AM – 1 PM                          Where: M Frierson Therapy | A Healing Space, 3601 Lee Road       Social Media:@mfr.sontherapyFamily fun day at Nevaeh's NestJoin Nevaeh's Nest for a Family Fun Day filled with games, music, activities, and summer fun for all ages on Saturday, June 27. The event will include carnival games, face painting, bounce houses, henna art, and more, along with an opportunity to learn about child care programs offered through Nevaeh’s Nest.When: Saturday, June 27 | 1 – 4p.m.Where:Nevaeh's Nest, 3591 Lee RdRaise a Glass at Blu Basil!Big news! Blu Basil Shaker Heights has officially received its liquor license and is now serving a full bar alongside several delicious new summer menu offerings. Whether you’re craving handcrafted cocktails, refreshing drinks, or fresh seasonal flavors, there’s never been a better time to visit.Address: 20126 Chagrin BlvdPhone: (216) 490-1177Website:https://theblubasil.com/Social Media:blu_basil_indiancuisineNow Open: Beloved Hearts Enrichment CenterThis new childcare center offers programs for children ages 6 weeks to 13 years old. The center provides infant, toddler, preschool, and before- and after-school programs, along with a state-approved curriculum, low child-to-teacher ratios, and CPR- and First Aid-certified staff.Address:Beloved Hearts, 3655 Lee Rd.Océanne Now Open at Van Aken DistrictOcéanne is now open at Van Aken District, bringing handcrafted jewelry, curated apparel, and thoughtful gifts to Shaker Heights. The Cleveland-based jewelry and lifestyle brand is known for French-inspired design, meaningful storytelling, and pieces created to celebrate connection, milestones, and everyday beauty.Find Océanne inside the Van Aken Market Hall and follow @oceannejewelry on Instagram to stay connected.KneadED Coming Soon to Shaker HeightsKneadED, a cooperative bakery and “third space” founded by Saidah Farrell and Adenike Harper, is coming soon to Shaker Heights! The concept brings together independent bakers, youth development, entrepreneurship, and community in one collaborative space.Follow KneadED on Instagram to join in the anticipation and stay connected as they prepare to bring this vision to life.Address:20106 Chagrin BlvdReclamation Space RentalReclamation, our neighborhood resale/consignment shop, is now offering its space for small community rentals. The intimate, flexible setting can be used for book clubs, meetings, craft nights, brand launches, pop-ups, performances, and other small gatherings, with tables, chairs, and audio equipment included. For bookings call: (216) 999-7508Email: contact@reclamationvintage.comVisit: reclamationvintage.comSocial Media:@shop.reclamationFrom Personal Journey to Van Aken BusinessesKait Turshen, owner of SLFMKR and Well Stocked in the Van Aken District, was recently featured by WKYC for the personal journey that led her to clean beauty and non-toxic home products - and to entrepreneurship. After navigating years of IVF and loss, Kait began looking more closely at the products she used every day, eventually inspiring her to bring curated clean beauty and clean living options to Shaker. Watch the full interview to learn more.EngageShop Shaker!Shop Shaker - our shop local campaign that showcases local businesses - has a fresh new look!  The updated logo reflects the local pride found throughout Shaker Heights’ business districts.  Shop Shaker will continue to highlight local businesses, events, openings, and ways to support our local business community.Follow @shopshakerhts on Instagram and on Facebook to stay connected and discover what’s happening throughout Shaker’s business community.4th Annual Chagrin-Lee Fest Set for August 29The Chagrin-Lee Fest will return on Saturday, August 29, from 12:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m. Hosted by the City of Shaker Heights, Shaker Heights Development Corporation, and partnering businesses, this year’s carnival-themed festival will feature live music, food trucks, family activities, vendors, and more as the community comes together to celebrate the end of summer in the Chagrin-Lee district. Save the date and join us!Vendor applications are also now open for makers, artists, small businesses, community organizations, and food vendors. Click here to apply and view additional event details.Business SpotlightsOrabi Orthodontics Brings Personalized Care to ShakerOrabi Orthodontics is a family-run practice at the Van Aken District in Shaker Heights led by Dr. Noha Orabi and her husband, Abe. With a focus on personalized care and a modern approach to treatment, they are building a practice centered on quality, comfort, honesty, and community.Connect: @orabiorthodontics and orabiorthodontics.comAddress: 3401 Tuttle Rd Garage Level 4 Suite 340Celebrate New Lee Road Murals!New public art is bringing more color and energy to Lee Road, with murals now installed at Elite Home Health Services (3649 Lee) and FASS Real Estate (3705 Lee). The two businesses are host sites for the project, helping create a more vibrant commercial district for residents, visitors, customers, and the broader community. Thank you Amy Williams, owner of Elite Home Health Services, and Akil Hameed, owner of FASS Real Estate, for your participation. The murals are part of the Lee Road Action Plan, adopted by Council in 2023, which called for projects that generate excitement in the district, including public art. Following an open call, the City’s Public Art Task Force selected Darius Steward and Snack Break Studio, artists Roni Callahan and Kim Lavery, for the project.Join us to celebrate the completed murals with an artist talk, gallery opening, and mural dedication.When: Wednesday, July 29 | 6 –8 PMArtist Talk and Gallery Opening:Shaker Main LibraryMural Dedication:3649 Lee Rd and 3705 Lee Rd, beginning at 7 PMRain Plan: The artist talk and gallery opening will continue as planned; the mural dedication will be postponed if needed.Development UpdatesLee Road Action Plan - Construction Begins this FallThe Lee Road Action Plan is moving into its next phase!  Cuyahoga County is managing the construction of "Complete Streets" infrastructure improvements, including roadway reconfiguration, utilities upgrades, a new bikeway, and streetscape improvements like landscapings, new trees, benches, bike racks, lighting and more.  At the end of May, Cuyahoga County awarded the construction contract to Perk Company, Inc. and CATTS Construction, Inc. Pre-construction planning is now underway, and construction is expected to begin this fall. Stay tuned for more details on construction phasing and detours.The project supports the community's vision for a more attractive, walkable, bikeable, and business-friendly district. Click here for regular updates on implementing the Lee Road Action Plan.Arcadia Rising on WarrensvilleConstruction is continuing on Arcadia, the five-story mixed-use development at the southeast corner of Warrensville Center and Farnsleigh roads. Recent project activity has included continued concrete work, framing, and utility coordination as the development moves toward completion.The development team expects pre-leasing to begin near the end of this year, with the first apartment homes anticipated to become available for move-in during spring 2027. For regular construction updates from the developer, visit buildingarcadia.com.Connect With UsWe Want to Hear From You! Laura EnglehartEconomic Development Director216.491.1334Georgina FigueroaEconomic Development Specialist216.491-1335Theodore Darden IVNeighborhood & Housing Specialist216.491.1333Dawn ArringtonNeighborhood Network Specialist216.491.1332Please do not reply to this email. The automated reply address will not reach us.  Email us at economicdevelopment@shakerheightsoh.gov with questions and comments. Share on Facebook  Share on Twitter  Share via Email Copyright City of Shaker Heights. All Rights Reserved.3400 Lee Rd., Shaker Heights, OH 44120 | 216-491-1400 If you no longer wish to receive emails from us, you may Unsubscribe. Powered byEmail not displaying correctly? View it in your browser.


